cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use PIGSTI, please cite this software (and the associated paper when
  available). Always record the exact release tag or commit SHA used for your run
  (see results/final/run_manifest.json).
title: "PIGSTI: a modular, reproducible pipeline for host identification and detection of ancient pathogens and zoonotic microbes in animal palaeogenomic data"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lhote
    given-names: Louis
    affiliation: "Trinity College Dublin"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-26"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/LouisLhote/PIGSTI"
url: "https://github.com/LouisLhote/PIGSTI"
keywords:
  - ancient DNA
  - pathogen detection
  - pathogen authentication
  - Snakemake
  - metagenomics
  - KrakenUniq
  - HOPS
abstract: >-
  Ancient genomics has enabled discovery of diverse pathogens across time periods,
  host species, and material types. PIGSTI (Pathogen anImal Genome Sequence ToolkIt)
  is a Snakemake pipeline for host identification and pathogen screening in shotgun
  data from ancient animal remains. It performs host mapping and pathogen
  identification with multi-criteria authentication, generating outputs suitable for
  population genetics and phylogenetic analyses.
